# The Sparkle 2 pin — ONE source of truth, read by BOTH consumers:
#   • cmake/Sparkle.cmake        (fetches the framework that gets embedded in the app)
#   • scripts/release/sparkle-tools.sh (fetches generate_appcast / sign_update)
#
# They must never disagree: an appcast signed by a tool from one release and verified
# by a framework from another is exactly the kind of mismatch that shows up only as
# "update rejected" on a user's machine, long after the build looked fine. Hence a
# shell-sourceable, cmake-parseable dotenv rather than two hardcoded copies.
#
# Bump both lines together. sha256 of the release tarball:
#   curl -sSL -o /tmp/s.tar.xz https://github.com/sparkle-project/Sparkle/releases/download/<v>/Sparkle-<v>.tar.xz
#   shasum -a 256 /tmp/s.tar.xz
MOSH_SPARKLE_VERSION=2.9.4
MOSH_SPARKLE_SHA256=ce89daf967db1e1893ed3ebd67575ed82d3902563e3191ca92aaec9164fbdef9
